    "is_free": true,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Math Attack is a mathematical puzzle game, built around the idea of using math operations to <i>attack</i> various expressions and reduce them to zero.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each level presents a new expression involving integers, irrationals, complex numbers, or even polynomials. Armed with a limited set of operations like subtraction, logarithms, and differentiation, your challenge is to determine the optimal order in which to apply them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are three categories of levels presented as folders in the level select: Real, Complex and Functions. Each category requires you to deduce certain properties of the expressions you work with.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With no tutorial or hand-holding, you're dropped straight into a mathematical labyrinth, left to uncover how each operation shapes the expressions before you. Trial, error, and insight are your only guides.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimalist Design</strong> \u2013 A clean and focused interface that keeps the math front and centre.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>39 Handcrafted Levels</strong> \u2013 Puzzles spanning three distinct mathematical domains: Real, Complex, and Functions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Built-in Info Tool</strong> \u2013 Peek under the hood of each expression and visualize how different operations affect it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Free-Form Level Selection</strong> \u2013 Tackle any level in any order. No restrictions, just exploration.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Undo &amp; Redo</strong> \u2013 Experiment freely with different strategies and operation sequences.</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Math Attack is a mathematical puzzle game, built around the idea of using math operations to <i>attack</i> various expressions and reduce them to zero.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each level presents a new expression involving integers, irrationals, complex numbers, or even polynomials. Armed with a limited set of operations like subtraction, logarithms, and differentiation, your challenge is to determine the optimal order in which to apply them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are three categories of levels presented as folders in the level select: Real, Complex and Functions. Each category requires you to deduce certain properties of the expressions you work with.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With no tutorial or hand-holding, you're dropped straight into a mathematical labyrinth, left to uncover how each operation shapes the expressions before you. Trial, error, and insight are your only guides.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimalist Design</strong> \u2013 A clean and focused interface that keeps the math front and centre.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>39 Handcrafted Levels</strong> \u2013 Puzzles spanning three distinct mathematical domains: Real, Complex, and Functions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Built-in Info Tool</strong> \u2013 Peek under the hood of each expression and visualize how different operations affect it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Free-Form Level Selection</strong> \u2013 Tackle any level in any order. No restrictions, just exploration.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Undo &amp; Redo</strong> \u2013 Experiment freely with different strategies and operation sequences.</p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Math Attack is a mathematical puzzle game about using math operations to reduce expressions to zero. Each level presents a clever numerical riddle hidden behind deceptively simple notation. It\u2019s a game of logic, foresight, and elegant solutions.",
